WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:06.930
The man known as Jackie Chan is one of the
biggest and most badass movie stars ever,

00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:11.660
and the first to bridge the gap between Hong
Kong action cinema and big-budget American

00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:12.160
movies.

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:17.880
Chan might be past 60, but he's still putting
his life on the line to thrill audiences.

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:19.440
Read the womb

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:25.499
Though it may seem like the big-screen legend
has been around forever, Jackie Chan was born

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:28.720
Chan Kong-sang in April 1954.

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:33.840
Nothing weird about that… until you realize
he was supposed to be born in January of that

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:34.340
year.

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:39.600
Yup, he hung out in his mother's womb for
a full 12 months before a British doctor had

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:41.100
to surgically remove him.

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:44.920
At the time of his forced birth, he weighed
12 pounds.

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:47.900
His mother nicknamed him Pao-Pao, or "cannonball."

00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:50.720
"My wife had such a difficult time delivering
him.

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:53.100
Afterward, she was totally exhausted.

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:57.240
The nurse brought the baby in, saying, "Aw,
he's so cute, just like a cannonball."

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:02.659
Nevertheless, that kind of medical procedure
isn't cheap, and Chan's parents couldn't afford

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:06.140
it; thus, they tried to sell their baby to
the doctor who delivered him.

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:08.220
The doctor said no obviously.

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:12.640
According to Chan's memoir, his parents gathered
the money from their friends and needed a

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:15.220
decade to pay them all back.

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:16.760
Learning from legends

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:23.119
When Jackie Chan was 7 years old, he was enrolled
and boarded at the China Drama Academy, where

00:01:23.119 --> 00:01:27.420
he was taught acting and singing in preparation
for a career in the Peking Opera.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:32.030
It was there that Chan lived and trained for
the next ten years, eventually forming an

00:01:32.030 --> 00:01:36.479
acrobatic troupe with some classmates called
the Seven Little Fortunes.

00:01:36.479 --> 00:01:41.630
Upon leaving school, Chan used the group to
gain his first roles in Hong Kong movies.

00:01:41.630 --> 00:01:46.659
He and the Seven Little Fortunes were extras
and stuntmen in Enter the Dragon and Fists

00:01:46.660 --> 00:01:51.380
of Fury, two of the most famous and popular
movies ever made by Bruce Lee.

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:55.140
Chan even got to spar on-camera with the screen
legend.

00:01:55.160 --> 00:02:01.580
"Suddenly, my eyes all black because he just
— one stick, right here, on my head."

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:05.760
Picky with voice parts

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:11.640
While a star in Asia since the 1970s, Jackie
Chan wasn't a mainstream star in the U.S.

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:15.610
until the release of Rumble in the Bronx in
1996.

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:20.000
Before that, he helped bring American movies
to Asia: for example, he provided the Mandarin

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:24.510
language voice acting of the Beast for the
Chinese dub of Beauty and the Beast.

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:29.691
Chan has since done voice work in the English-language
releases of other major animated movies, one

00:02:29.691 --> 00:02:34.740
notable example being his portrayal of Master
Monkey in the Kung Fu Panda movies.

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:39.620
However, you might be surprised to hear of
the one place he didn't lend his voice: the

00:02:39.620 --> 00:02:42.240
cartoon series Jackie Chan Adventures.

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:46.500
Although he appeared in live-action bumpers
for the show, the cartoon version of Jackie

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:48.220
Chan is voiced by James Sie

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:50.720
"But I don't know anything about Children!"

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:54.500
who also, incidentally,
took over as Master Monkey in the TV series

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:56.600
spinoff of Kung Fu Panda.

00:02:56.980 --> 00:03:01.890
To make things even more confusing, the character
of Jade Chan, Jackie's fictional niece on

00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:06.200
the series, was voiced by Stacie Chan, Jackie
Chan's real-life niece.

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:07.960
No stranger to danger

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:13.680
After starring in dozens of martial arts and
action movies in which he's done his own stunts,

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:16.440
Jackie Chan has sustained a number of injuries.

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:22.430
So much so that in 2013, his movie Chinese
Zodiac was promoted in Japan with a poster

00:03:22.430 --> 00:03:27.290
that consisted of an image of Chan's body
with arrows pointing to all of his injured

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:28.040
body parts.

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:31.480
Among the injuries Chan has suffered in the
pursuit of entertainment:

00:03:31.780 --> 00:03:36.180
On Drunken Master, he damaged a bone behind
his eyebrow, and it nearly blinded him.

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:39.440
On City Hunter, he dislocated his right shoulder.

00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:45.200
On The Armour of God, Chan fell out of a tree
and suffered a skull fracture, a bone cave-in

00:03:45.210 --> 00:03:47.980
behind the ear, and bleeding into his brain.

00:03:47.980 --> 00:03:51.160
During surgery, bone chips were removed from
his head.

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:52.160
"Two fingers.

00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:57.860
"I'm bowling with Jackie Chan."

00:03:57.860 --> 00:03:58.760
"Oh my god — Yes!

00:03:58.760 --> 00:03:59.260
Yes!

00:03:59.340 --> 00:03:59.840
Yes!"

00:04:00.580 --> 00:04:03.520
He broke his breastbone on Armour of God II.

00:04:03.530 --> 00:04:08.360
During the filming of The Accidental Spy,
he broke his tailbone and was temporarily

00:04:08.360 --> 00:04:09.000
paralyzed.

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:14.120
Oh, and he's broken his nose four separate
times: once while making The Young Master,

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:18.960
once on Project A, once on Miracles, and once
on Mr. Nice Guy.

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:22.520
Ouch we'll never complain about a stubbed
toe again!

00:04:22.520 --> 00:04:24.620
"Broken, broken, teeth gone.

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:26.400
Jaws, cheek.

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:28.180
Broken, broken, broken.

00:04:28.180 --> 00:04:30.360
Crack, crack, crack, crack, crack."

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:32.320
The 1,000th time's the charm

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:37.420
Directors may require a lot of takes to get
a scene the way they want it.

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:42.220
In one example of this borderline abusive
practice, Stanley Kubrick infamously required

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:47.200
Shelley Duvall to film one scene in The Shining
127 times.

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:53.000
By that logic, the most sadistic director
that Jackie Chan has ever worked with is … himself.

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:57.979
While directing and starring in the 1982 movie
Dragon Lord, a sequence in which characters

00:04:57.979 --> 00:05:03.080
play "jianzi" a Chinese sport similar to hacky
sack, but with a weighted, badminton-style

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:06.360
shuttlecock just didn't look right to director
Chan.

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:13.070
It's been reported that the scene took 2,900
takes, but it probably didn't take that many.

00:05:13.070 --> 00:05:18.870
The book Kung Fu Masters places the number
over 190, and other estimates come in at over

00:05:18.870 --> 00:05:19.380
1,000.

00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:22.480
Either way, Chan was dedicated to the shot.

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:24.460
Tough love

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:28.500
Jackie Chan's a movie star, which means he's
rich.

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:32.430
He's amassed a fortune of more than $350 million.

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:37.069
In addition to earning salary and box office
percentages from his films, he's owned a chain

00:05:37.069 --> 00:05:39.700
of movie theaters and a Segway dealership.

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:42.680
And when he dies, a lot of that is going to
charity.

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:48.980
But his son, Jaycee Chan who was convicted
on drug charges in 2015 stands to inherit

00:05:48.980 --> 00:05:50.460
exactly none of that.

00:05:50.849 --> 00:05:56.240
In 2011, Chan publicly mentioned that he won't
leave his fortune behind to his son, remarking:

00:05:56.240 --> 00:05:58.780
"If he is capable, he can make his own money.

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:02.220
If he is not, then he will just be wasting
my money."

00:06:02.760 --> 00:06:06.360
It seems like there's a little more to the
story than that — especially considering

00:06:06.380 --> 00:06:10.180
the fact that their relationship isn't without
its past bumps in the road.

00:06:10.360 --> 00:06:15.800
Jackie once even admitted that he had beaten
Jaycee when he was a child, admitting that

00:06:15.820 --> 00:06:17.370
he was not a "model father."

00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:20.640
But it looks like threats of violence are
off the table these days…

00:06:20.840 --> 00:06:25.520
"Wearing the white shoes, running around — because
he don't wash his own shoes.. socks!"

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:26.160
"Do you give him a shot?"

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:28.080
"No, I can't — he'll sue me!"

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:30.040
Polarizing politics

00:06:30.540 --> 00:06:35.100
While Jackie Chan boasts fans from every corner
of the globe, he's still very loyal to his

00:06:35.110 --> 00:06:37.969
home nation of China's political system of
communism.

00:06:37.969 --> 00:06:43.189
In fact, he's way more politically outspoken
then most of his fans probably realize.

00:06:43.189 --> 00:06:47.370
He's even opened up about his opinions on
the American way of life on more than one

00:06:47.370 --> 00:06:47.900
occasion.

00:06:48.060 --> 00:06:49.240
In 2013, he said:

00:06:49.640 --> 00:06:53.540
"What I can see is [China] continuously making
progress and learning.

00:06:53.550 --> 00:06:58.029
If you talk about corruption, the entire world,
the United States, has no corruption?

00:06:58.029 --> 00:07:00.699
[It's] the most corrupt in the world."

00:07:00.699 --> 00:07:03.020
But his opinions don't end with the US.

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:08.210
In 2009, he talked about the dangers of too
much freedom in China-controlled Taiwan, saying:

00:07:08.480 --> 00:07:12.960
"I don't know whether it is better to have
freedom or to have no freedom.

00:07:12.969 --> 00:07:15.370
With too much freedom, it can get very chaotic.

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:17.540
It could end up like in Taiwan.

00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:21.680
Chinese people need to be controlled; otherwise,
they will do whatever they want."

00:07:21.880 --> 00:07:26.300
Whether you agree or disagree with Chan's
beliefs, one thing's for certain: he knows

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:30.639
how to get pulses racing no matter where his
fans fall on the political spectrum!

